# Design: the S-series simplification method

## Problem
V0.9 accumulated ~25 player-facing rules. The user asked for
simplification without losing strategic challenge, so cuts needed
evidence, not taste.

## Approach
A web research pass produced one test: a rule stays only if
removing it changes measured play. Each suspect rule was screened
by deletion on 96 matched seeds with the frozen gates, then the
combined trim ran on 384 fresh seeds against 0.9.0.

## Key Trade-offs
- Duel boost and first-challenger bonus cut: identical metrics,
  two fewer lines of text and two fewer incentive hooks.
- Six abilities kept: collapsing them widens the strategy spread
  (S1 collector 0.39 / farmer 0.10), so the identities carry
  balance, exactly what the playtest wanted.
- Contest fee kept: fee 0 returns 60% draws even with window and
  shame - the strongest keep signal in the series.
- Guard posts kept as income floor: cut pressure exists, but
  zero-Prestige seats must keep a priced move (death-spiral and
  kingmaking literature).

